10.1 Add HTTP Cookie Manager
The HTTP Cookie Manager allows JMeter to store and send cookies just like a real browser. This is critical for handling login sessions and maintaining user state across requests.
Steps:
Right-click on your Thread Group
Navigate to:
Add → Config Element → HTTP Cookie Manager
No extra configuration is needed for basic usage
📌 Tip: Enable the option "Clear cookies each iteration" if you want each virtual user to simulate a fresh session on every loop.
10.2 Add HTTP Cache Manager
The HTTP Cache Manager simulates browser caching behavior, which helps make performance testing more accurate for web apps that utilize static resources and cache-control headers.
Steps:
Right-click on your Thread Group
Navigate to:
Add → Config Element → HTTP Cache Manager
Default configuration is sufficient for most use cases
